# Internal design notes (HLD/LLD/LOGIN) stay out of the repo; the public ChatGPT-submission
# docs under docs/chatgpt/ are a deliverable and are tracked. Written as docs/* rather than
# docs/ because git cannot re-include a path inside an excluded DIRECTORY.
docs/*
!docs/chatgpt/
!docs/submission/
.idea/
Documents/
AI Responses/
manual response/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored `build-page-schemas/` also matched
# `.claude/skills/build-page-schemas/`, which left 13 of that skill's 16 reference files
# untracked while SKILL.md and two references were committed — the skill's rules were
# half under version control, and a stale duplicate of the whole skill grew at the root.
/build-page-schemas/
/emit-schema-to-cms/
/frontend/
/schemas/
# The Page Builder's working history: output/<SITE_KEY>/ holds the plan, census, raw pages,
# extracts, library.md, trace.json, merge-log.md, the emit plan/report and the frontend build
# report. Resumable and debuggable, but not a deliverable -- the durable handoff is the three
# files in /schemas/<SITE_KEY>/.
/output/
# Local-only env profile for running this server on localhost (see local.env)
local.env
# Direct CDS/CMS Basic Auth credentials for manual testing outside MCP (see local-credentials.env)
local-credentials.env
# Anchored for the same reason as the block above: an unanchored `next/` also matched
# the top-level next/ app itself, silently excluding the whole build-cms-frontend
# deliverable (every next/sites/<SITE_KEY>/ build) from version control entirely.
# next/node_modules is already handled by next/.gitignore.
.claude/skills/build-cms-frontend/scripts/node_modules/
/build-cms-frontend/
/csv files/
test.md
.claude/skills/verify-visual-fidelity/scripts/node_modules/
